`[host]` **New task from the owner, read-only: inventory the games on the console's storage and cross-reference them with xemu's compatibility list.** It runs ahead of your queue, unless the full6743 console run is mid-flight, in which case finish that run first. The owner has set 1.0 as a games target: 90% of the 950 titles xemu rates Playable or better must be playable on the handhelds, with about 145 titles validated per minor version. The first question is which of the 950 we can get onto a handheld at all.

**The list.** `/home/justin/hakux-work/titles/xemu-compat-2026-09-25.csv` (and `.json`) holds 1,104 titles, 950 of them Playable or Perfect. It was built from `https://reports.xemu.app/compatibility` and xemu's `xdb` title names. Columns:
- `title_id` and `canonical_title_id`: 8 hex digits, as the XBE certificate stores them;
- `name`, `xemu_rating`, `xemu_rank` (xemu's own display ranking, 1-150);
- `regions`, `report_date`;
- `playable_or_better`.

**The job (FTP listing and partial reads only):**
1. List every partition you can reach (C, E, F, G and any extended ones) and find every game: each folder with a `default.xbe`, and any `.iso`/`.xiso` file.
2. For each `default.xbe`, read its certificate (partial download with `REST` is enough):
   - base address at 0x104;
   - certificate address at 0x118, so the file offset = cert − base;
   - title ID at cert+0x08;
   - the title name, UTF-16LE, 40 chars, at cert+0x0C;
   - game region flags at cert+0xA0.
3. Match each game on `title_id`, then on `canonical_title_id`.
4. Write `/home/justin/hakux-work/titles/console-inventory-2026-09-25.csv` with these columns: `drive, path, kind (folder|iso), size_bytes, title_id, xbe_title_name, region_flags, xemu_name, xemu_rating, xemu_rank, playable_or_better`. Unmatched rows get empty xemu columns.
5. Post a summary on #112:
   - how many games, how many matched, and how many of those are Playable or better;
   - the total size of the matched Playable+ set;
   - whether the games are folders (they would need repacking to XISO for the handhelds) or ISOs.

**Constraints:**
- Read-only: no writes, no launches, no reboots, whatever the state of the power switch.
- If the switch is in, say so on #110 as well. The host notes it on your board row.
- The handhelds' storage is the host's side. Don't touch them.

